{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfqZWXB3WJbRiG4U8iZ3b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All eight rows in this sitting are now approved and anchored: seven re-attested and TC-330 approved for the first time. Each step is its own commit, ending with `WI: WI-846`.\n\n| Commit | What it holds |\n|---|---|\n| 67523d0a | The verdict `002-ADJUDICATE-6a34e67.md`: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=7`, `OUTCOME: APPROVE rows=1`, `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment;first-approval` |\n| 46ff9e18 | The amendment act: `snapshot --reattests` for SR-227, LLR-270, LLR-305, TC-267, TC-268, TC-323 and TC-324. No cell or `Status` changed. |\n| a999b8e9 | The first-approval act: TC-330 moved from `Drafted` to `Approved` (that one line only), plus `snapshot --approves \"docs/test/test-cases.toml=WI-846\"` |\n\n**Amendment: every row changed meaning, and I would bless every new text.** The lane's rewrite (6a34e674) fixed each problem the first sitting raised:\n- **SR-227:** the ordinary-home refusal is fully stated again: when it refuses, that it names the setup step, and that there is no automatic sign-in and no fallback.\n- **LLR-270 and TC-267:** nothing says \"as before\" any more. The tombstone protocol, the lock-exclusion assertion, the leftover-file assertion and the dedicated-Codex-home assertions are all back.\n- **LLR-305:** the exact Codex and Claude sign-in outputs are listed again, along with the rule that a missing home is never created.\n\n**First approval: TC-330 is ready.** Its Expected cell now claims only the guarantee that SR-227 and decisions D-002 and D-004 support, and its Method names all 16 tests. I checked that the tests really cover argv and commits: `test_the_token_is_read_at_launch_and_never_logged` asserts a fake token value is absent from argv, printed output, the telemetry commit and every file the run writes.\n\nTwo non-blocking notes are in the verdict:\n- **LLR-270:** removing a first call's l